[h2]Vending Machine Enhancement (Modules & Capacity)[/h2]
In the base game, neither the Vending Machine nor the Vending Fountain has a module bay, Vending Machine capacity tops out at 10 narrow upgrades (8×12), and reopening either machine always snaps its window back to the center of the screen. This mod gives both machines full module support, doubles Vending Machine capacity with wider shelves, and fixes window position memory.

[list]
[*][b]Full Module Bays for Both Machines[/b]: Adds a dedicated module bay to both the Vending Machine and the Vending Fountain. Drag a [b]Module Bay Expansion Kit[/b] directly onto either machine's core to expand its bay up to 2 times.
[*][b]Meaningful Efficiency, Performance & Quality Effects[/b]:
  - [b]Efficiency[/b]: Reduces nightly power draw on both machines (including extra power from capacity and attractiveness upgrades).
  - [b]Performance[/b]: Scales effective attractiveness on the Vending Machine to raise nightly sale odds for all stock, and continues scaling guaranteed nightly sales past 100 attractiveness (+1 guaranteed sale per extra 50 by default, configurable in Mod Config). On the Vending Fountain, adds extra nightly water sale rounds (+1 guaranteed round per +100%, with partial percentages rolling for an extra round).
  - [b]Quality[/b]: Stacks extra sale price markup on top of the base +10% bonus for both machines using the configured Quality coefficient (10% by default, up to 100% in Mod Config). [b]Note: Quality only boosts payout price and does not increase attractiveness or sale chance.[/b]
[*][b]Doubled Vending Capacity (Up to 14×16)[/b]: Raises Vending Machine capacity upgrades from 10 to [b]20[/b]. Upgrades 1-10 follow vanilla (8×2 to 8×12), while upgrades 11-20 widen and heighten the grid up to [b]14×16 (224 cells)[/b]—more than double vanilla's 96-cell limit. (Vending Fountain water storage is unchanged.)
[*][b]Actionable Tooltips & Window Position Memory[/b]: Hover items inside the Vending Machine to see exact projected sale payouts (or whether an item is ineligible). Hover either machine core to inspect effective attractiveness and guaranteed sales, nightly water sale rounds, total price bonus, current grid size, and module bay upgrade progress. Both machines now remember where you moved their windows instead of snapping back to center every time.
[/list]

[h3]Options[/h3]
Fine-tune balance and compatibility anytime under [b]Options -> Mod Config[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]Quality Effect (%)[/b] (default: 10%, range: 0-100%): Scales how much Quality converts into extra sale price markup for both machines. Set to 0 to keep only the base +10% bonus.
[*][b]Performance Effect (%)[/b] (default: 100%, range: 0-300%): Scales Performance's effect on vending attractiveness and nightly water sale rounds. Set to 0 to disable it.
[*][b]Guaranteed Sale Step (Over 100)[/b] (default: 50, range: 0-500): Extra attractiveness needed per +1 guaranteed sale above 100 effective attractiveness. Set to 0 to keep the vanilla cap of 3.
[*][b]Enable 20-Level Capacity Expansion (up to 14×16)[/b] (default: On): Turn off to let vanilla or another vending capacity mod handle shelf size while keeping module bays and window position memory.
[/list]

[h3]Compatibility & Notes[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Sale & Guaranteed Sale Rules (Important)[/b]: Guaranteed nightly sales follow the vanilla game rule—[b]only non-luxury items with a retail-marked-up price of 50 or less qualify[/b] (prioritizing consumables such as food and drinks). Pricier items such as injectors, tools, modules, and luxury goods [b]are excluded from guaranteed sales[/b] and rely solely on random nightly roll odds; additionally, when stocking duplicates of the same item ID, vanilla halves each extra copy's chance to enter that night's roll pool. To reliably sell higher-value goods, upgrade base attractiveness with electronics and install [b]Performance modules[/b] (and optionally raise [b]Performance Effect (%)[/b] in Mod Config) to push effective attractiveness into the hundreds—for example, a single tool or standard item priced at 100 reaches 100% roll chance at 300 effective attractiveness.
[*][b]Mod-Friendly Design[/b]: Compatible with multi-machine and restock mods such as [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3836658488]More Vending Machines[/url]. Window position memory hooks window centering instead of blocking store clicks, nightly sales only swap the attractiveness lookup, core tooltips append cleanly without overwriting, and the 20-level capacity expansion can be toggled off anytime in Mod Config.
[*][b]Existing-Save Friendly[/b]: Appends the module bay at the end of the panel list so existing slot indices stay intact; machines in existing saves migrate and recalculate automatically on load.
[*][b]Before Disabling[/b]: Remove any modules from the added module bays—and move Vending Machine stock placed outside the vanilla 8×12 grid—before disabling or uninstalling this mod so nothing is lost.
[*][b]Zero Sensitive Capabilities[/b]: Declares empty Capabilities (no external reflection).
[/list]

